<title>SPAIN: Spain names head of telecommunications commission.</title>
<headline>Spain names head of telecommunications commission.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Development Minister Rafael Arias Salgado said on Tuesday he would propose Secretary General for Communications Jose Maria Vazquez Quintana as head of the new National Telecommunications Commission.</p>
<p>Salgado made the announcement to parliament's infrastructure commission and said the appointment would be made effective during the next regular cabinet meeting.</p>
<p>The commission's main task will be to arbitrate competition criteria in the Spanish telecommunications market, which is due to be liberalised by 1999.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
